disassembler
============

The native Rust walker (walker/) and the intra-accession haplotype-recovery
method were written by Andrew (@as042), building on an earlier Rust port
of a Python prototype path walker. Both were developed in an earlier
repository; their history was squashed into a single import commit here, and the
design and measurement record that matters for users is kept under docs/
(see docs/issue_intra_accession_variance_lost.md and
docs/issue_graphaligner_end_clipping.md).

The k-mer diversity sieve under extern/kmer-diversity-sieve is a separate project,
https://github.com/stevenweaver/kmer-diversity-sieve, included as a git submodule
under its own license.
